cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Cross-sectional intratumoral microbial abundance cannot establish causation: a calibration study using an established carcinogen as a natural control"
abstract: >-
  A validation study showing that the two significance tests most commonly
  reported in tumor microbiome analyses both pass on data constructed to
  contain no biological signal, and that in a decontaminated reference cohort
  an established carcinogen is depleted rather than enriched at the tumor site.
  Extends to a two-sample Mendelian randomization screen of 211 gut taxa with
  independent replication in 100,204 colorectal cancer cases.
type: software
